      "message": "if this participates in ThinLTO, it\u0027s possible for `DefaultReallocate` to be inlined, which would allow LLVM to conditionally \u0027see through\u0027 some values of `ptr`.\n\nTo be safe it can be sanitized through a volatile:\n\n```suggestion\n    if (size \u003c\u003d old_size) {\n        // Store \u0026 load this through a volatile so LLVM can\u0027t infer an\n        // objectsize for FORTIFY through it. Ideally, there should instead\n        // be a `__builtin_assert_object_size(ptr, size)` or similar, but until\n        // then, \"we don\u0027t know the size,\" is more correct than \"the size is the\n        // same as if the realloc never happened\"\n\tvoid *volatile v \u003d ptr;\n        return v;\n    }\n```\n\n(feel free to reword the comment)\n\n(or you can add a `noinline` attr)",
